    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-fa11c38a3019\",\"class\":\"not\",\"constraints\":[],\"coverage\":\"\",\"residual\":\"Does the code in this hunk pad or encrypt a NIP-44 v2 plaintext without first checking that its length is at least 1 byte and at most 4294967295 bytes, so that an empty or oversized plaintext is accepted?\",\"probes\":null,\"rationale\":\"Answering this means showing that a check is missing. The checker would have to see that a pad or encrypt call works on a NIP-44 plaintext, then confirm no correct length check guards it anywhere in the hunk. That check could be spread over several lines or done by a helper with any name. A regex applied line by line cannot prove such absence or follow data flow, so no literal pattern decides any part soundly.\"}",
